# The Android SDK archives that `setup.sh install android` installs, one line per host and package:
#
#   <host> <package path> <version> <archive> <sha256> <sha1>
#
# host: setup.sh's android_host (linux is x86_64). archive: a path below Google's repository
# (dl.google.com/android/repository/). sha256: what setup.sh checks, computed from the archive when
# it was pinned. sha1: Google's own checksum from its repository listing (repository2-3.xml,
# sys-img/google_apis/sys-img2-4.xml), which the archive matched then; `-` for the emulator 37.2.12,
# which the listing no longer offers (it lists only the newest builds).
#
# To move a pin: download the archive, check its SHA-1 against the listing, put its SHA-256 here.
# A changed line changes the saved copy's name (setup.sh artifact android), so CI fetches and saves
# the new set once (.github/workflows/README.md, "Android SDK").
#
# cmdline-tools 22.0, not 23.0: 23.0's sdkmanager hands over to the new "Android CLI", which
# downloads itself into ~/.android and collects usage data unless told not to. setup.sh never runs
# sdkmanager to install (22.0's also says it is deprecated): it unzips these files itself.
# emulator 37.2.12: a known build under the device suite, not whatever Google released last (37.2.13
# came out mid-way through the suite's first CI runs); both crashed alike with one GPU mode
# (apps/server/test/devices/android.ts EMULATOR_GPU).
